  "result": "Summary of UTC-aware date utilities:\n\n**`src/dates.js`** (new module)\n- `isValidDate(dateString)`: Validates 'YYYY-MM-DD' format and checks for valid dates\n  - Rejects invalid formats and impossible dates (Feb 30, etc.)\n  - Uses UTC for all date validation\n- `addDays(dateString, n)`: Adds n days to a date (n can be negative)\n  - Returns new date in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n  - Handles month/year boundaries correctly\n  - All arithmetic in UTC\n- `daysBetween(a, b)`: Calculates days between two dates (b minus a)\n  - Returns whole days as integer (using Math.floor)\n  - Handles month/year boundaries and leap years\n  - All arithmetic in UTC\n\n**`src/invoices.js`** (updated)\n- Imported `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed internal `isValidDate()` function\n- `createInvoice()` now uses centralized date validation\n\n**`test/dates.test.js`** (new test file - 17 tests)\n- Valid date acceptance and format validation\n- Invalid format rejection\n- Impossible date handling (Feb 30, non-leap Feb 29)\n- Leap year logic (2000\u2713, 1900\u2717, 2024\u2713, 2023\u2717)\n- `addDays()` with positive/negative/zero values\n- Month and year boundary crossing\n- `daysBetween()` positive and negative differences\n- Large date range calculations\n- Leap year edge cases\n- Inverse relationship verification (addDays/daysBetween roundtrip)\n\n**Test Results:** 111/111 passing \u2713\n\nAll date operations use UTC exclusively; no local timezone dependencies anywhere in the date handling.",
